      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we hold that there is no Bivens action for First Amendment retaliation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77aca25def67fac2c73605cc5f4633d292b5449bbc6616d69d09bf9a6609c853",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77aca25def67-0002-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, more recently, we have indicated that if we were called to decide Bivens today, we would decline to discover any implied causes of action in the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77aca25def67fac2c73605cc5f4633d292b5449bbc6616d69d09bf9a6609c853",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77aca25def67-0002-0005",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our Constitution's separation of powers prohibits federal courts from assuming legislative authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77aca25def67fac2c73605cc5f4633d292b5449bbc6616d69d09bf9a6609c853",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77aca25def67-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there \u201cany reason to think that Congress might be better equipped\u201d than a court to \u201c `weigh the costs and benefts of allowing a damages ac- tion to proceed' \u201d?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "77aca25def67fac2c73605cc5f4633d292b5449bbc6616d69d09bf9a6609c853",
      "evidence_id": "ev-77aca25def67-0002-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "boils down to a \u201csingle question\u201d: Is there \u201cany reason to think that Congress might be better equipped\u201d than a court to \u201c `weigh the costs and benefts of allowing a damages ac- tion to proceed' \u201d?"
    },
